117
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:58,160
Well, what this process did was it made it more important to have more meetings between professors and students.

118
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:01,920
So a student would present their doctoral project, their doctoral proposal.

119
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,680
And that's a fairly articulated process.

120
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:06,160
They have to have a bibliography and a direction to go.

121
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:08,880
A board of professors sits with the student.

122
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:11,520
They work it out, approve it or change it whatever.

123
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:22,640
Then the student has to return after the first piece of research and say if the student is writing in Italian and you know the quality of the person's Italian and now the student is writing like Dante.

124
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:26,720
Knowing the student, you know what's happened.

125
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:34,720
So if when you have regular meetings, instead of waiting till the dissertation is finished, you can challenge the student with the content that the student has written.

126
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,160
Do you understand what you've written?

127
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,600
What are the implications of this?

128
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:50,640
And so you have a more interpersonal focus in the educational process and the student has to defend, even if they've used whatever AI tools, the student has to defend what he or she has written.

129
00:12:51,360 --> 00:13:01,200
So oddly, the technology has improved human communication, which is the last thing we always expect.pect with AI and digitization.

130
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:18,640
Another thing, the benefit that it offers is there have been mistakes made academically in the past for clear reasons that can now be researched in a more clear, concise and quick way.

